@startuml
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam roundcorner 6
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFF0
skinparam noteBorderColor #BA7517

title Fault sequence — network lag and message reorder

participant "Client\nclient.py" as C
participant "Network\n(lagged)" as N
participant "Server\nserver.py" as S

C -> N : PUSH {direction: d, seq=1}  — sent first
C -> N : PUSH {direction: s, seq=2}  — sent second

note over N #FFD580
  Network lag delays seq=1.
  seq=2 arrives at server first.
end note

N -> S : seq=2 arrives FIRST
S -> S : apply_move(s)\nlast_move_seq[id] = 2

N -> S : seq=1 arrives SECOND
S -> S : apply_move(d)\nlast_move_seq[id] = 1

S --> C : PUB state after seq=2 applied
S --> C : PUB state after seq=1 applied

C -> C : wait_for_my_move(seq=2)\nlast_seq >= 2 confirmed

note over C, S
  Result: moves applied in arrival order,
  not send order. Final player position
  differs from intended sequence.
  Demonstrates reorder vulnerability.
  Prototype does not correct this.
end note
@enduml